To efficiently find the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2 using MATLAB, you can use the following code:
```
% Read text files
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt');
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt');
% Convert text to lowercase and split into words
words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));
% Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);
% Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);
```
This code reads two text files (in this case, 'Text1.txt' and 'Text2.txt'), converts them to lowercase, splits each word into individual elements, finds the unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2 using `setdiff`, and prints the result.
This approach should be efficient for most cases, as it only requires reading the text files once, converting the text to lowercase, splitting it into words, finding the unique words, and printing the result. However, if you need to process very large amounts of text, you may want to consider parallel processing or other optimization techniques.

